# Design system primitives (app)

Import from `@denser/design-system`. Full rule: `.cursor/skills/frontend-patterns/rules/design-system-primitives.md`.

## Defaults

| Need | Use | Avoid |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Scrollable list / menu / panel | `ScrollArea` with explicit height (`h-56`, `h-64`, `h-full min-h-0`) | `overflow-y-auto` / `overflow-auto` on wrappers |
| Scrollable `DropdownMenuContent` (list only) | `max-h-*` on content (built-in `overflow-y-auto`) | Nested `ScrollArea` |
| Dropdown with fixed header + scroll list | `min-w-0 overflow-hidden` on content, `h-*` on `ScrollArea`, `w-*` on row anchor | `w-*` on content when using `ScrollArea` |
| Tabs | `Tabs`, `TabsList`, `TabsTrigger`, `TabsContent` | Hand-rolled tab strips |
| Actions / triggers | `Button` | Raw `<button>` for product chrome |
| Option picking | `Select` (+ trigger/content/items) | `<select>`, `NativeSelect` (except native-form exceptions) |
| Message timelines | `MessageScroller` | `ScrollArea` on chat lists |

## ScrollArea in menus

List only — use built-in menu scroll:

```vue
<DropdownMenuContent class="w-56 max-h-64">…</DropdownMenuContent>
```

Header + scrollable list — width on the row anchor, not the shell:

```vue
<DropdownMenuContent class="min-w-0 overflow-hidden">
  <DropdownMenuLabel class="shrink-0">Section title</DropdownMenuLabel>
  <ScrollArea class="h-64">
    <div class="flex flex-col">
      <DropdownMenuItem v-for="item in items" :key="item.id" as-child>
        <RouterLink :to="item.to" class="flex w-56 min-w-0 items-center">
          <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate">{{ item.label }}</span>
        </RouterLink>
      </DropdownMenuItem>
    </div>
  </ScrollArea>
</DropdownMenuContent>
```

`min-w-0` on `DropdownMenuContent` lets the `ScrollArea` viewport shrink; `w-56` on each link sets the column width so `truncate` ellipsizes correctly.

## Exceptions

- Virtualized or DS-owned scroll roots (`MessageScroller`, etc.)
- `overflow-hidden` for clipping only (not scrolling)
- `NativeSelect` only when native semantics are intentional (calendar internals, documented form exceptions)
